  "latest_nl_proof": "Let x be any real number with 0 \u2264 x. By the definition of the floor function, floor(x) is the greatest integer m such that m \u2264 x. Since 0 is an integer and 0 \u2264 x, the integer 0 is a candidate in this set. Therefore the greatest integer m \u2264 x cannot be smaller than 0. Hence floor(x) \u2265 0.",
